      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Peralta Adobe, built in 1787, is San Jose’s oldest Spanish structure and the last tangible remnant of Pueblo de San José.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sjdowntown.com/history-walk/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic De Anza Hotel, the Fairmont Hotel, and the San Jose Museum of Art line the downtown core, each telling a chapter of the city’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Downtown_San_Jose",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A self‑guided walking tour in downtown lets drivers pause at QR‑coded markers that reveal stories of San Jose’s shift from a farming community to a Silicon Valley hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sjdowntown.com/history-walk/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The City purchased the historic De Anza Hotel in 1966, restored it in 1976, and now preserves its architectural and historical significance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
